Privacy Policy for Hardware Catalog Automation
Last Updated: April 2026

This Privacy Policy describes how the Hardware Catalog Automation tool ("the App") handles data when connecting to the Pinterest API. This tool is an internal automation solution designed to manage product catalogs for a sanitary hardware business.

1. Data Collection
The App does not collect, store, or share any personal data from Pinterest users. The only data accessed is related to the authenticated user's own account (e.g., boards and pins) for the purpose of managing business content.

2. Use of Data
The App uses the Pinterest API specifically to:

Create and update Pins for sanitary hardware products.

Organize products into relevant Pinterest Boards.

Sync product descriptions and images from our internal database to Pinterest.

3. Data Storage and Security
No Third-Party Sharing: We do not sell, trade, or share any data accessed via the Pinterest API with third parties.

Local Processing: The App runs on a private instance (via n8n). All authentication tokens and API keys are stored securely within the user's private environment and are never exposed publicly.

4. User Control
Since this is an internal tool, the only user is the administrator. You can revoke the App’s access at any time through your Pinterest account settings under "Apps."

5. Contact
For any questions regarding this automation tool, please contact the developer via the GitHub profile associated with this repository.
